{
  "title": "Filestorage",
  "uid": "system-4015",
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "rgba(255, 96, 96, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tags": [
    "onboarding",
    "platform"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "Environment",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "PROD : prod",
        "current": {},
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "System",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Filestorage** (`4015`, type `platform`)\n\nTenant: `4015-${env}`\n\nOwner: Platform Engineering (platform-team@example.com)\n\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Configured Ingestion Budget",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 9,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**PROD**: 30 GB total (1 GB/day x 30 days retention, size `S`)\n\nRendered from the manifest at generation time - not a live query. See **Ingestion Budget Usage** alongside for the live percentage."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Ingestion Budget Usage (per Signal)",
      "description": "This tenant's real ingested volume since local midnight (Europe/Zurich), as a percentage of EACH signal's own daily budget - Metrics (Mimir), Logs (Loki), Traces (Tempo), Profiles (Pyroscope) each shown as its own line. Both values read directly from two gauges scripts/ingestion-midnight-snapshot.py pushes every 2 minutes (demo_ingestion_since_midnight, demo_ingestion_daily_budget) - no subtraction on this panel's own side (NFR-05 SECOND pre-test audit round, fixed here: this used to recompute \"current minus a separately-pushed day-start snapshot\" in this panel's OWN PromQL, independently of - and able to silently disagree with - the enforcer's own decision, with its own version of that script's pre-fix reset-insensitivity; both now read the exact same, already-correct value). Green below 80%, yellow 80-90%, red above 90%. Same formula as the Operator: Tenant Ingestion Budget dashboard's own panel, filtered to this one tenant. Queried via the Mimir-anonymous datasource, not Mimir-4015-${env} - see README.md's Multi-Tenancy section for why (self-monitoring metrics land under the anonymous tenant).",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-anonymous",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 17,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 120,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 80
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "expr": "100 * demo_ingestion_since_midnight{tenant=~\"4015-${env}\"} / on(tenant, signal) demo_ingestion_daily_budget{tenant=~\"4015-${env}\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{signal}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 50,
      "title": "Storage Operations Rate by Type",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (operation) (rate(storage_operations_total{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "title": "Bytes Throughput by Operation",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (operation) (rate(storage_operation_bytes_sum{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 52,
      "title": "Average Operation Size by Type",
      "description": "rate(storage_operation_bytes_sum) / rate(storage_operation_bytes_count) - mean payload size per operation type.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (operation) (rate(storage_operation_bytes_sum{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}[5m])) / sum by (operation) (rate(storage_operation_bytes_count{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 53,
      "title": "Total Storage Used",
      "description": "Current total bytes across all blobs in the container (storage.container.bytes gauge, updated on every \"list\" cycle in workload.py). Blobs are only ever added, never deleted, so this trends upward - watch Daily Growth Rate alongside for anomalies.",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": "Mimir-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "storage_container_bytes{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 54,
      "title": "Total Blob Count",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": "Mimir-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "storage_container_blob_count{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 55,
      "title": "Daily Growth Rate",
      "description": "Growth of storage_container_bytes over the last 24h - a sudden jump or drop here is the anomaly signal to watch for. max() first merges the series of old and new pods after a rollout into one curve; within the first 24h after a (re)build it estimates the growth from the samples available so far (delta() extrapolates). The trailing \"and max(...)\" hides the panel when the metric is no longer reported.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "delta((max(storage_container_bytes{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"}))[1d:1m]) and max(storage_container_bytes{k8s_pod_name=~\".+\"})",
          "legendFormat": "growth (24h)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Recent Traces",
      "description": "A table, not the \"traces\" panel type - Grafana's traces panel silently renders zero rows when Tempo's search response omits durationMs (happens for very fast, sub-millisecond traces), even though the underlying data is there. A table shows the same rows regardless.",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": "Tempo-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{} with (most_recent=true)",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Log Volume by Namespace",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Loki-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (k8s_namespace_name) (count_over_time({k8s_namespace_name=~\".+\"}[$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{k8s_namespace_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Recent Logs",
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": "Loki-4015-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{k8s_namespace_name=~\".+\"}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
